Establishes the weekly operational-observation lane after the independently verified bounded live canary.

Scope:
- schedule a weekly revalidation at 16:17 UTC Sundays;
- retain an explicitly confirmed manual dispatch for repair/testing;
- pin target commit `d9abc05fa648f8b2049fb443477bc8f97691cf7f`;
- bootstrap from verified canary run 32487223314, then chain only from the latest successful weekly artifact;
- stream-verify every incoming CAS object before acquisition;
- revalidate the complete reviewed 500-work inventory against the live service;
- reconcile exact identities, CAS, cumulative manifest/checkpoint accounting, and write explicit state lineage;
- retain complete success/failure state for 90 days.

Expected outcome:
Each elapsed cycle produces a real source-backed, cumulative, independently reconcilable state artifact. Multiple successful elapsed cycles—not workflow configuration alone—will be required before the weekly gate is complete.

Risk/failure modes:
- missing/expired state, missing source credential, corrupt CAS, incomplete source responses, reconciliation mismatch, or malformed receipts fail closed;
- concurrency is serialized and each cycle is capped at 180 minutes and 500 works;
- no publication, rights clearance, target cutover, or donor archival is authorized.

Validation:
- 203 tests passed;
- Ruff format and lint passed;
- `git diff --check` passed.

The donor remains unarchived.
